<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Irish NTMA variable rate auction covered 4.12times.</title>
<headline>Irish NTMA variable rate auction covered 4.12times.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ireland's National Treasury Management Agency (NTMA) said on Monday that its auction of 150 million Irish pounds of the variable rate bond due 2000 was covered 4.12 times.  </p>
<p>The NTMA said the highest accepted price was 100.27, the lowest accepted price was 100.20 while the average price accepted was 100.23.</p>
<p>The agency said that 25 percent of each bid was allocated at the lowest price of 100.20.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
</text>
